<title>FRANCE: Valeo reaffirms 1996 sales forecast.</title>
<headline>Valeo reaffirms 1996 sales forecast.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French car parts maker Valeo reaffirmed on Thursday its target of reaching turnover of 28.5 billion francs for the full year 1996, thanks to strong activity at the start of the second half.</p>
<p>&quot;The start of the second half was marked by strong activity in all markets. Barring any reversal of this trend, Valeo should achieve its objective of turnover of 28.5 billion francs in 1996,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Valeo posted 1995 turnover of 25.23 billion francs. In the first half of 1996, it had sales of 15.06 billion compared to 13.02 billion a year ago. cct/ylg/pnt</p>
